  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "brief",
      "x": 1260,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "text": "Three asks, one flow.\n\n1. Find icons \u2014 17 marks, one style, three sizes. Sketched here; the ImageGen lane paints them from the brief under each.\n2. The bag \u2014 things stop applying themselves on reveal. They go in the bag; you use them when you like. Currencies and homes still land directly.\n3. Dismiss \u2014 X with no actions just closes. X with actions asks once, says what waits and what's kept, and never loses a dig. The receipt is the only exit after the end.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "entry-choice",
      "x": 1260,
      "y": 2620,
      "w": 380,
      "text": "Where the bag lives \u2014 pick one.\n\nA (in the flow above): a third option in the Barn button's fan. Keeps the yard clean; the fan already knows dig / barn. Badge on the closed button. Tradeoff: one tap hidden.\n\nB (left): a satchel sticker hung in the yard, always visible, badge on it. Tradeoff: the yard is already carrying a stamp, a coin, a mound and a button.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "dismiss-rules",
      "x": 1260,
      "y": 330,
      "w": 390,
      "text": "Dismiss rules\n\u00b7 0 actions \u2192 X closes, no sheet.\n\u00b7 actions \u2192 this sheet. Keep digging is primary; leave for now is the hand link.\n\u00b7 leaving snapshots + syncs; the Barn button reads 'your dig waits \u00b7 closes in 3h'.\n\u00b7 after tie / wake / cap, the receipt is the only way out; its X = Back to the Barn.\n\u00b7 no swipe-to-dismiss on the full screen.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "tally-chosen",
      "x": 660,
      "y": 900,
      "w": 860,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Chosen 2026-09-13: the tally receipt (A), and this woke treatment.\n\nThe grammar: before \u2192 now on a sun sticker (cream2 when he woke); one ledger row per find, landing ~350 ms apart, each +n rolling the top number; a truffle he took reads 'his' with no number; 'the dig \u00b7 +n' on the foot; Back to the Barn; the hand link (share the dig \u203a / next time \u2014 tie it at the mud?). Things still land where they live (shelf, Barn, Burrow Book, wardrobe) \u2014 that's the row's sub line, never a second reward.\n\nSet aside (page 3): B tumble-out, C weigh-in, D stamp, and A1\u2013A5. Worth borrowing later: B's tickle burst on the Barn stamp when you land back in the yard."
    }
